WEBVTT

1
00:00.400 --> 00:03.630
If your ERP runs on IBM i,

2
00:03.680 --> 00:08.730
years of orders, customers, items and invoices are already there.

3
00:09.630 --> 00:13.340
Your team gets answers from ERP screens and reports,

4
00:13.390 --> 00:16.460
from Excel, and from BI dashboards.

5
00:16.510 --> 00:19.880
Each one handles the questions it was built for.

6
00:20.780 --> 00:25.510
Then there's the one-off question that nobody has built a report for yet.

7
00:27.010 --> 00:29.813
Now your team can ask it in plain language,

8
00:29.863 --> 00:34.480
in an AI assistant such as Claude, and get the answer from live data,

9
00:34.530 --> 00:36.220
with the numbers.

10
00:38.320 --> 00:43.150
Sales, purchasing, service, manufacturing, finance.

11
00:43.200 --> 00:45.850
Ask the questions you actually have.

12
00:49.100 --> 00:53.350
With Claude for Excel, the answer goes straight into your sheet.

13
00:55.450 --> 01:01.267
Your IT team can write down what an open order or an active customer means at your company,

14
01:01.317 --> 01:05.140
so the assistant uses your definitions instead of guessing.

15
01:06.240 --> 01:08.030
It only reads.

16
01:08.080 --> 01:10.457
Everyone signs in as themselves.

17
01:10.507 --> 01:14.510
Your IT team chooses what's visible, every request is logged,

18
01:14.560 --> 01:17.850
and nothing is copied into a new database.

19
01:18.750 --> 01:21.607
Your IT team sets it up once.

20
01:21.657 --> 01:24.700
Official figures still come from your finance reports.

21
01:24.750 --> 01:27.480
This is for the questions in between.

22
01:29.530 --> 01:31.720
It's free and open source.

23
01:31.770 --> 01:34.180
Send this page to your IT team.
